; ── Rewards ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

; Antique silver necklace (granted with ADJ1=851 antique, ADJ2=292 silver) —
; everyone who claims a share. It starts unenchanted;
; RUB activates whatever spell a GM imprints on it (@editem: VAL3 = spell
; number, VAL2 = charges), the same mechanism as other rub-to-cast jewelry, so
; it can take over the role of a player's existing enchanted necklace. Charge
; Wand (243) can recharge it once it has a spell.
INUMBER 9344
NAME 141
MISC
WORN_NECK
WEIGHT 1
VOLUME 1
SUBSTANCE SOFTMETAL
*DESCRIPTION_START EXAMINE
A fine silver chain from which hangs a tarnished medallion. Engraved on it, in astonishing detail, is the skyline of Old Fayd as it stood before the Cataclysm: towers and domes that no living person has seen. On the back, tiny letters read, "Remembered."
*DESCRIPTION_END
IFVERB RUB -1
  IFITEM -1 WORN
    IFVAR ITEMVAL3 > 0
      ECHO ALL %N's antique silver necklace glows softly.
      ROUTINE 1
    ENDIF
  ENDIF
ENDIF
;
; Marren Vey's Lantern Charm — everyone who claims a share. Granted with
; VAL3=113 (Light) and VAL2=50 charges; RUB to cast. Rechargeable with Charge
; Wand (243).
INUMBER 9345
NAME 1021
ADJECTIVE 1163
MISC
WEIGHT 1
VOLUME 1
SUBSTANCE SOFTMETAL
*DESCRIPTION_START EXAMINE
A tiny charm shaped like a hooded lantern, no longer than your thumb, worked in tarnished silver. It is cold with the memory of Old Fayd. When you hold it close, you could swear you smell lamp oil and wet earth.
*DESCRIPTION_END
IFPREVERB RUB -1
  CLEARVERB
  ECHO PLAYER You rub the tiny lantern charm, and a pale golden light kindles inside it.
  ECHO OTHERS %N rubs a tiny lantern charm, and a pale golden light kindles inside it.
  ROUTINE 1
ENDIF
;
; Engraved funeral ring — GM-awarded to the first finder of each leg
; (@additem 9346 adj1=115 → "an engraved funeral ring", then @give).
INUMBER 9346
NAME 167
ADJECTIVE 9309
MISC
WORN_RING
WEIGHT 1
VOLUME 1
SUBSTANCE SOFTMETAL
*DESCRIPTION_START EXAMINE
A heavy ring of dark silver. Its bezel is engraved with the symbol of the Old Fayd Cemetery: a broken obelisk beneath a hooded lantern. Inside the band are the words "He kept faith."
*DESCRIPTION_END
